messages:
anya: Quick accessibility note from the dashboard filter panel review. Two issues: dynamic result count isn't announced to screen readers when filters change, and the 'Clear filters' ghost button has a near-invisible focus ring in high-contrast mode.
phil: Repro steps for count?
anya: Focus anywhere -> change a filter (checkbox / dropdown) -> visible count updates (e.g., 124 -> 97) but VoiceOver/NVDA silent. Users relying on AT won't know results changed.
rowan: Sounds like we need an aria-live region for the count or to announce the new value after filter changes. Prefer minimal: a polite live region that updates with a succinct string like "97 results".
keiko: Agree. Implementation idea: put a visually-hidden element with role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" near the filter controls and set its text to `${count} results` after debouncing updates by 300ms.
anya: Also noticed the Clear filters text button uses a 1px outline of subtle grey on focus which disappears in high-contrast. Auto-scan shows focus outline contrast ~1.5:1 in HC theme. Screenshot: https://attachments/reports/filter-clear-focus.png
phil: For focus visibility we should use a thicker outline and a stronger color. Proposal: outline: 2px solid var(--focus-strong); outline-offset: 3px. On HC theme pick #FFD966 which hits ~3.3:1.
rowan: Back to live region: be careful to not spam announcements on every rapid change (slider drags etc). Debounce and coalesce identical values. Also avoid announcing when the panel is hidden.
keiko: Example helper:

```
// debounce updates and avoid duplicate texts
let lastAnnounced = '';
function announceResults(count) { 
  const text = `${count} results`;
  if (text === lastAnnounced) return;
  lastAnnounced = text;
  const el = document.getElementById('a11y-filter-count');
  if (!el) return;
  el.textContent = text;
  setTimeout(() => { el.textContent = ''; lastAnnounced = ''; }, 1200);
}
```
anya: Tests: unit for presence of live node and aria attributes; e2e keyboard flow: tab into filter, toggle a checkbox, expect live node to contain new text; visual snapshot for focus ring in HC and dark theme.
phil: Also add aria-label on the Filter toggle button: aria-label="Open filters" + aria-expanded toggling. Lots of folks assumed it was decorative.
rowan: Good catch. And make sure the filter panel traps focus when open and returns focus to toggle on close.
a11y_bot: Auto-scan summary: missing aria-live for dynamic count, Clear button focus ring fails HC contrast, missing aria-label on Filter toggle in some variants. Recommend fix + CI e2e keyboard + HC visual snapshots.
keiko: I'll open a small PR with: (1) live region node and announce helper with debounce, (2) thicker high-contrast focus ring + CSS var, (3) aria-label + aria-expanded on toggle, (4) tests (unit + e2e). Assign to @phil for review.
phil: Thanks 44d please ensure the live text is short and consistent across locales (i18n string key).
anya: Good point 44c we'll use i18n key "filters.results_count" with interpolation.
rowan: Also note mobile screen-reader behavior might read the toast; ensure we don't duplicate announcements on mobile. Add a small guard for window.innerWidth < 480 to use a single shorter announcement.
keiko: Added that to the PR branch. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/redwood/pull/5422 - includes screenshots and test updates.
anya: Reviewing now. Marking resolved after merge. :white_check_mark:
